A relative `--target` resolves against the workdir and stands in for the machine's declared
`artifact:`. The declared path is seeded here too, and stays at its own status: the move lands on
the target only.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-run
title: Run
summary: Hookless states-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  intake: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: researching
            when: intake complete
      researching:
        transitions:
          - to: done
            when: research complete
      done: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/intake/prompt.md --
---
summary: Intake the request.
---

Intake body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: intaking
---
-- fixtures/cwd/run/review.md --
---
status: intaking
---
-- cmd --
booping playbook-transition fx-run researching --target review.md --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
intaking → researching
frontmatter: status=researching
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/review.md --
---
status: researching
---
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: intaking
---
